        "en-ocr-degraded": "Below release: on the degraded scan Tesseract reads 3.75 as 3:75 -- a speck of the scan's salt noise sits above the decimal point. The neural engine removes specks from each line before reading it; Tesseract reads the page whole, and a page-wide speck filter would take one pen for every line (on the Arabic page the footer's dots, area 9 with its own pen 3, sit just above the body pen's speck size, 8: a smaller type would lose its dots). Every word is right (CER/WER count words, not the punctuation inside them), so numbers OCR'd from poor scans are not qualified with Tesseract."
